Name: frameDuration

Type: property

Syntax: get the frameDuration of <image>

Summary:
Reports the display duration of the current <frame> of an <animated GIF>
in milliseconds.

Associations: image

Introduced: 1.0.0

OS: mac, windows, linux

Platforms: desktop, server

Example:
send "nextFrame" to me in (the frameDuration of image "myGIF") milliseconds

Value:
The <frameDuration> of an <image> is a <non-negative> <integer>
representing milliseconds.
This property is read-only and cannot be set.

Description:
Use the <frameDuration> <property> to obtain the delay time specified
for the current <frame> of an <animated GIF>. The value is expressed in
milliseconds and reflects the timing encoded in the GIF file.

Set <currentFrame> before reading <frameDuration> to obtain the duration
for a specific frame.

If the image is not an animated GIF, <frameDuration> returns 0.

References: property (glossary), animated GIF (glossary),
frame (glossary), non-negative (glossary), image (keyword),
integer (keyword), currentFrame (property), frameCount (property),
frameText (property), frameImageData (property), repeatCount (property)

Tags: multimedia
